{
  // Alloy furnace, a crucible furnace under a chimney: the anchor model of a 3x3x3 multiblock, authored in
  // 0..48 model units (three cells on every axis, the anchor cell's origin at 0) with the firemouth on the
  // NORTH (-Z) face. ContentRegistry pre-rotates the bake to the other three facings (MultiblockShape.Rotate),
  // so this file is the only orientation ever written by hand. The same bake rules as the mud brick kiln hold:
  // no face carries a "cullface", and no face covers a whole cell face.
  //
  // No face declares "uv": the baker's defaults follow the element's position, so the bricks run on across
  // elements, and the copper course (alloy_band repeats every 2 units) sits on even heights.
  //
  // The shape, bottom to top: a plinth (y 0..4), the body (inset 3, y 4..30) between four corner buttresses
  // standing on the full footprint (y 4..26), a copper course (inset 2, y 30..32), two roof tiers (inset 7 to
  // y 37, inset 12 to y 41) and the chimney (x/z 17..31, y 41..48) around a sooty well. The block's
  // multiblock.boxes (data/blocks/alloy_furnace.json) trace the same pieces.
  //
  // The firemouth is x 10..38, y 5..24, z 0..36 - cell space [0.625,2.375] x [0.3125,1.5] x [0,2.25], the
  // numbers KilnLayout.Furnace mirrors - under a stepped vault (x 14..34 up to y 28) and behind a frame standing
  // two units proud of the body. The crucible stands on a pedestal (x 18..30, z 10..22, top at y 8) with the
  // firebox floor around it. Every face omitted below is buried inside another element.
  "textures": {
    "brick": "alloy_bricks",
    "hearth": "fired_mud",
    "band": "alloy_band",
    "soot": "kiln_soot"
  },
  "elements": [
